    24	    //TEMPLATE VALUE: This is a just a simple example for setting up quick notices
    25	    const OPTION_KEY_NEW_NOTICE_TEMPLATE        = 'duplicator_new_template_notice';
    26	    const OPTION_KEY_IS_ENABLE_NOTICE_DISMISSED = 'duplicator_is_enable_notice_dismissed';
    27	    const OPTION_KEY_IS_MU_NOTICE_DISMISSED     = 'duplicator_is_mu_notice_dismissed';
    28	
    29	    const GEN_INFO_NOTICE    = 0;
    30	    const GEN_SUCCESS_NOTICE = 1;

Phase 1 signals were traced in source. No Patchstack-eligible exploit path survived refutation: capability gates are present on the flagged package/tools/web-service flows, the nopriv one-click-upgrade path is gated by an export-only OTH handshake, and the capability-less notice/toolkit endpoints did not expose a meaningful lower-privilege path.
  ✓ Extract candidate entry points and anomalies from duplicator Phase 1 artifacts
  ✓ Trace each high-value candidate in source code, validate defenses, and refute or confirm exploitability
  → Write reports/phase2/duplicator-phase2.codex.json with evidence-backed findings and review notes
